@@ -125,6 +125,17 @@ The page refreshes itself every 20 seconds, so new bot bookings appear on their
 
 **Editing the dashboard code** (needs Node.js): `cd dashboard`, `npm install`, `npm run dev` (live preview at http://localhost:5173). When done, run `npm run build` (the backend serves `dashboard/dist`).
 
+## 6c. Phone-call reminder (Exotel, optional)
+About **2 hours before** each visit the backend rings the patient's mobile through Exotel and plays a short reminder.
+It reaches every patient with a mobile number, also walk-ins without Telegram.
+- Fill the `EXOTEL_*` values in `.env` (see `.env.example`), then restart. `python check_setup.py` tests the keys.
+- Exotel → App Bazaar → create a flow **Greeting → Hangup** and put its ID in `EXOTEL_FLOW_ID`.
+  - Now (on your PC): use **fixed text** in the Greeting, e.g. "Namaste. This is City Clinic, Kota. This is a reminder about your appointment in about two hours. Please check Telegram for details. Thank you."
+  - After deployment: switch the Greeting to **text from URL** = `https://<your-site>/api/public/exotel/greeting` – it then says the patient's name, doctor, time and booking ID.
+- One call per booking (a reschedule allows a new one), only between 8 am and 9 pm, at most `CALL_DAILY_LIMIT` calls a day.
+- The dashboard shows "Call reminder <time>" or "Call reminder failed" under the appointment status.
+- **Trial account:** calls go only to numbers verified in Exotel (max 10), the trial lasts about 7 days, and credits are limited.
+
 ## 7. Optional: Cal.com webhook
 
 This tells patients when staff cancel or move a booking inside Cal.com.
